只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DeepSeek Harness direct-connect module for a local SekaiSync knowledge base — 10 compact tools, zero dependencies.","id":"gh:1388365419","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-sekaisync-connect","slug":"omoinoki/dsh-sekaisync-connect","topics":["cordis","deepseek-harness","dsh","dsh-plugin","knowledge-base","pjsk","project-sekai","prsk","sekaisync","zero-dependency"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness direct-connect module for a local SekaiSync knowledge base — 10 compact tools, zero"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ss direct-connect module for a local SekaiSync knowledge base — 10 compact tools, zero dependencies."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# SekaiSync Connect for DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"[](package.json) [](package.json) [](package.json) [](LICENSE)"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Overview ·\nQuick start ·\nConfiguration ·\nPlugins panel ·\nTools ·\nUsage ·\nMore information"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"A **DeepSeek Harness direct-connect module** for the SekaiSync knowledge base: zero dependencies, ze"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"ro build steps, and minimal token usage — plus a Plugins-panel page for choosing the deployment path"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"o build steps, and minimal token usage — plus a Plugins-panel page for choosing the deployment path."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Installation"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Requires **Python ≥ 3.10** with a working `python -m sekaisync` (no third-party dependencies), plus "},{"id":"p8s2","text":"a\nsynced store (a `sekaisync init` / `sync` product)."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Project home: <https://github.com/omoinoki/dsh-sekaisync-connect>"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| Runtime | Verdict |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"| `0.1.x` | **DENY** — the panel API this plugin needs does not exist before `0.2.0-rc.1` |\n| `0.2.0"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"-rc.1` | allow (verified: tools, panel, and a real lookup all run on this runtime) |\n| `0.2.0-rc.2` "},{"id":"p12s3","text":"| allow (verified: real Web profile, deployment panel, tool execution, and scoped facts) |\n| `0.2.x`"},{"id":"p12s4","text":" | allow |\n| `0.3.0` / `0.3.0-rc.1` / `1.0.0` | **DENY** — unverified versions fail closed |"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Anything outside the allowed range is refused rather than half-loaded, so the worst case is a clear\n"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"\"incompatible\" notice instead of a crash. To run an unverified version anyway, use\n`dsh plugin allow"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"ble\" notice instead of a crash. To run an unverified version anyway, use\n`dsh plugin allow-version`."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"If a runtime upgrade ever disables this plugin, the symptom is that the tools disappear entirely and"},{"id":"p14s2","text":" the\npanel stops loading — the whole bundle is rejected before any of its code runs."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"## Configuration"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Precedence: **environment variables > profile row config > `SEKAISYNC_CONFIG` file > plugin-director"},{"id":"p16s2","text":"y `config.local.json` > `config.json` > automatic discovery**."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"| Setting | Description |"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"| `SEKAISYNC_STORE` | Store directory containing `kb/`. When omitted, discovery checks `<SEKAISYNC_R"},{"id":"p18s2","text":"OOT>/store`, cwd/store, and the repository store located with `python -c \"import sekaisync\"` |\n| `SE"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"KAISYNC_ROOT` | SekaiSync repository root, used as the working directory for `python -m sekaisync` |"},{"id":"p18s4","text":"\n| `SEKAISYNC_PYTHON` | Python executable; defaults to `python` |\n| `SEKAISYNC_PORT` | Port to probe"},{"id":"p18s5","text":" for an existing server; defaults to 8787. If a ready SekaiSync service is already listening there, "},{"id":"p18s6","text":"it is reused instead of starting another process. 0 retains its meaning: skip the external probe and"},{"id":"p18s7","text":" start a managed service directly |\n| `SEKAISYNC_MAX_RESPONSE_BYTES` | Byte budget for one successfu"},{"id":"p18s8","text":"l HTTP response; defaults to 134217728 (128 MiB), configurable from 65536–1073741824. It can also be"},{"id":"p18s9","text":" set as `maxResponseBytes` in a configuration file or profile row. Exceeding the budget cancels the "},{"id":"p18s10","text":"read and returns an explicit error |"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"You can also override these settings in your own profile patch; plugin upgrades do not overwrite tha"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"also override these settings in your own profile patch; plugin upgrades do not overwrite that layer:"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Keep the row `id` as `sekaisync-connect`. It is the key the panel writes through, so if you copy thi"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"s\nsnippet into a profile that still uses an older id, update that row's id to match — otherwise the "},{"id":"p21s3","text":"panel\nand the saved path refer to different rows."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"- HTTP connects only to loopback and rejects redirects. Health and error responses are limited to 64"},{"id":"p22s2","text":" KiB and 4 KiB respectively. The default successful-response budget is 128 MiB, covering typical bod"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"y results with `limit=100` and `max_text_chars=200000`. `max_text_chars=0` still means full text ups"},{"id":"p22s4","text":"tream; if an exceptionally large full-text response exceeds the transfer budget, increase `maxRespon"},{"id":"p22s5","text":"seBytes` (up to 1 GiB) or read in batches.\n- External-port reuse still follows the existing `/health"},{"id":"p22s6","text":"` ready/status check. That endpoint carries no store identifier, so you must ensure the configured p"},{"id":"p22s7","text":"ort serves the intended knowledge base."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"## Choosing the deployment path in the Plugins panel"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"When a Web profile serves the client, the plugin also appears as a **Configure** page on its row und"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"er **Plugins** in the sidebar. That page selects the SekaiSync deployment from the GUI instead of ed"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"he sidebar. That page selects the SekaiSync deployment from the GUI instead of editing JSON by hand."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Open **Plugins → Installed → dsh-sekaisync-connect → the row's Configure control**. The page offers:"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"| Control | What it does |"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"| Path field + **Check** | Classifies the path and reports whether it is a store, a repository root,"},{"id":"p27s2","text":" or a `kb/` directory — plus database size, `kb/` entry count, and the `freshness` payload when pres"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"ent |\n| **Save and apply** | Validates the path, then persists it through the official `settings` se"},{"id":"p27s4","text":"rvice into the profile's `cordis.patch.yml` and applies it live — the effective `store` / `root` rea"},{"id":"p27s5","text":"dout updates immediately, no restart required |\n| **Test connection** | Performs a real `/health` re"},{"id":"p27s6","text":"quest against the selected deployment and reports latency and readiness |"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"The **Effective store** / **Effective root** readout tracks the path field as you type (debounced),\n"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"and shows a **Not saved yet** marker whenever the typed path differs from the saved one — so a chang"},{"id":"p28s3","text":"e\nis visible before you commit to it."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"A store can live outside the source repository. Without neighboring SekaiSync source files,\nthe pane"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"l preserves the configured `root` instead of replacing it with the data parent.\nA recognized source "},{"id":"p29s3","text":"repository can select a new root. If no root is configured, the parent\nremains an explicitly unverif"},{"id":"p29s4","text":"ied fallback for an installed Python package; use **Test connection**\nto check the selected deployme"},{"id":"p29s5","text":" fallback for an installed Python package; use **Test connection**\nto check the selected deployment."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"The panel reads and writes the plugin's own **Cordis Config** (`store` / `root`), so a change surviv"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"es\nupgrades and takes effect without restarting DSH. The value shown is what the runtime resolves af"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"ter the\nfull precedence chain: environment variables > profile row config > `SEKAISYNC_CONFIG` >\n`co"},{"id":"p30s4","text":"nfig.local.json` > `config.json` > automatic discovery."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"Constraints, by design:"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"## Tools"},{"id":"p34s1","text":"Ten model-facing tools, all read-only against the local knowledge base:"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"| Tool | Cost | Purpose |"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
